# Must-fail mutant for legacy-invoices.schemas.test.ts (AC-2/AC-9, T48).
#
# Mutates the declared `pagination.offset` default (design.md §8.11's
# declared mutation point for the schemas unit specification, D-24) — drops
# the `default` key outright, so ajv's `useDefaults` leaves it unset.
#
# Reds: legacy-invoices.schemas.test.ts — "@AC-9 declares its OWN limit
# default of 10 and offset default of 0" (`model.pagination?.offset` reads
# `undefined`, not `0`).
#
# Declared collateral: NONE, empirically verified against design.md §8.11's
# own prediction. Design.md §8.11 predicts this patch also reddens the AC-9
# page-window-write INTEGRATION specification's offset-fallback half, on the
# claim that "the offset zero comes from the module's own declaration, never
# the query core" (D-24). That claim does not hold at runtime: the actual
# fallback the integration specification observes is
# `packages/headless/src/modules/query/useQuery.ts:421`'s own
# `criteria.props.value.pagination?.offset ?? PAGINATION.offset` —
# `PAGINATION.offset` is `query.utils.ts`'s own hard-coded constant, read
# independently of this module's schema declaration. Verified two ways: (1)
# dropping the schema's declared default outright, as this patch does, still
# leaves `pnpm --filter @upmind-automation/headless test:integration
# legacy-invoices.collection` fully green (14/14) — the integration
# fallback is unaffected; (2) CHANGING the declared default's VALUE (tried
# and discarded: `default: 5`) does NOT redden the AC-9 integration
# assertion either, and instead reddens an UNDECLARED, unrelated
# specification — "@AC-4 the next-page move ... the previous-page move
# returns the already-fetched first page from cache" — because ajv's
# `useDefaults` fill leaks the mutated value into an intermediate
# `setCriteria` merge during page navigation, producing a spurious cache
# miss. That value-mutation was REJECTED for exactly the reason a broadly-
# or wrongly-red mutant is a broken control; this drop-the-default mutation
# is the one shipped, because it reddens ONLY its own named assertion.
# **This is a finding for the operator, not a fix applied here**: design.md
# §8.11's and ruling AC9-FIX's premise that "AC9's fallback anchor stays on
# this module's own declaration, never on the query core" does not match the
# shipped wiring for the OFFSET default — the query core's own constant is
# the true anchor, regardless of what this schema declares.
#
# Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/legacy-invoices/legacy-invoices.schemas.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/legacy-invoices/legacy-invoices.schemas.ts
@@ -103,9 +103,9 @@
       pagination: {
         type: "object",
         additionalProperties: false,
         properties: {
           limit: { type: "integer", minimum: 0, default: PAGINATION.limit },
-          offset: { type: "integer", minimum: 0, default: PAGINATION.offset }
+          offset: { type: "integer", minimum: 0 }
         }
       }
     }
